[Event "KIA vs the French"]

{The King's Indian Attack is a system: e4, d3, Nd2, Ngf3, g3, Bg2, O-O, Re1. White attacks on the kingside with e5 and h4.}
1. e4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
1... e6 {The French. Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
2. d3 {[%csl Ge4] The KIA: avoid the French theory. Supports the centre: the pawn on d3 controls c4 and supports the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1.}
2... d5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and eyes the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
 (2... c5 {Black delays ...d5. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 controls b4 and d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
3. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and d4.}
3... Nc6 {Develops the knight to c6, where it controls d4 and e5.}
4. g3 {Same KIA setup: Bg2, O-O, Re1. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
)
3. Nd2 {Supports e4. Develops the knight to d2, where it supports the pawn on e4.}
3... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it supports the pawn on d5 and eyes the pawn on e4.}
4. Ngf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and d4.}
4... c5 {Space. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 controls b4 and d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
5. g3 {Fianchetto. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
5... Nc6 {Develops the knight to c6, where it controls d4 and e5.}
6. Bg2 {The bishop on the long diagonal. Fianchettoes the bishop on g2, where it rakes the long diagonal through f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
6... Be7 {Develops the bishop to e7, where it controls d6 and supports the knight on f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8. Re1 {[%csl Ge5] Supports e5. The rook goes to e1 and supports the pawn on e4.}
8... b5 {The queenside attack begins. Gains space on the queenside; the pawn on b5 takes a4 and c4 away from the opponent.}
 (8... Qc7 {Black adds pressure to e5 in advance. The queen goes to c7 and controls e5.}
9. Qe2 {[%csl Ge5] Over-protects e5 before pushing. The queen goes to e2 and supports the pawn on e4.}
)
9. e5 {[%cal Ge5f6] Kicks the knight and gains kingside space. Claims the centre: the pawn on e5 controls d6 and eyes the knight on f6.}
9... Nd7 {Moves the knight out of attack to d7 and eyes the pawn on e5. White's last move put a pawn on e5, which this now pressures.}
10. Nf1 {[%csl Gh2,Gg3] The knight heads for h2 or g3 to support h4–h5.} *

[Event "KIA vs the Sicilian & Caro-Kann"]

{The same setup works against 1...c5 and 1...c6.}
1. e4 {Claims the centre: the pawn on e4 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d1 and the bishop on f1.}
1... c5 {The Sicilian. Supports the centre: the pawn on c5 controls b4 and d4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
 (1... c6 {The Caro-Kann. Supports the centre: the pawn on c6 controls b5 and d5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
2. d3 {The KIA approach. Supports the centre: the pawn on d3 controls c4 and supports the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1.}
2... d5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and eyes the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c8 and the queen on d8.}
3. Nd2 {Supports e4. Develops the knight to d2, where it supports the pawn on e4.}
3... e5 {Black builds a centre. The pawn on e5 controls d4 and f4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
4. Ngf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls d4 and eyes the pawn on e5. That pawn is currently undefended.}
4... Bd6 {Develops the bishop to d6, where it supports the pawn on e5.}
5. g3 {Fianchetto. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
5... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it supports the pawn on d5 and eyes the pawn on e4. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
6. Bg2 {Long diagonal. Fianchettoes the bishop on g2, where it rakes the long diagonal through f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
6... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... Re8 {Supports ...e4 ideas and e5. The rook goes to e8 and supports the pawn on e5.}
8. Re1 {Supports e4; e4xd5 or Qe2 next. The rook goes to e1 and supports the pawn on e4.}
)
2. Nf3 {Develops the knight to f3, where it controls e5 and d4.}
2... e6 {Supports the centre: the pawn on e6 controls d5 and f5. It also opens a line for the queen on d8 and the bishop on f8.}
 (2... Nc6 {Develops the knight to c6, where it controls d4 and e5.}
3. d3 {KIA setup. Supports the centre: the pawn on d3 controls c4 and supports the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1.}
3... g6 {Closed-Sicilian style fianchetto. The pawn on g6 controls f5 and h5.}
4. g3 {Mirrors. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
4... Bg7 {Long diagonal. Fianchettoes the bishop on g7, where it rakes the long diagonal through f6, e5 and d4.}
5. Bg2 {Long diagonal. Fianchettoes the bishop on g2, where it rakes the long diagonal through f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
)
3. d3 {The KIA setup. Supports the centre: the pawn on d3 controls c4 and supports the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the bishop on c1.}
3... Nc6 {Develops the knight to c6, where it controls d4 and e5.}
4. g3 {Fianchetto. The pawn on g3 controls f4 and h4.}
4... d5 {Claims the centre: the pawn on d5 controls c4 and eyes the pawn on e4. It also opens a line for the queen on d8.}
5. Nbd2 {Supports e4. Develops the knight to d2, where it supports the pawn on e4.}
5... Nf6 {Develops the knight to f6, where it supports the pawn on d5 and eyes the pawn on e4.}
6. Bg2 {Long diagonal. Fianchettoes the bishop on g2, where it rakes the long diagonal through f3. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
6... Be7 {Develops the bishop to e7, where it controls d6 and supports the knight on f6. That clears the way to castle kingside.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8. Re1 {[%csl Ge5] Prepares e5. The rook goes to e1 and supports the pawn on e4.} *
